Source: hyperv
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: hyperv-for-linux maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/olljanat-ai/hyperv-for-linux

Package: hyperv-hypervisor
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: Microsoft Hypervisor binary (repackaged from Azure Linux non-oss)
 Ships the closed-source hypervisor loader (hvloader.efi) and supporting
 binaries under /usr/lib/hyperv/. Repackaged from the RPMs published at
 packages.microsoft.com/azurelinux/3.0/prod/non-oss/.

Package: hyperv-firmware
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: Firmware blobs required by the Microsoft Hypervisor
 Installs firmware files under /usr/lib/firmware/hyperv/ that the
 hypervisor loads at boot.

Package: hyperv
Architecture: amd64
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 hyperv-hypervisor (= ${binary:Version}),
 hyperv-firmware (= ${binary:Version}),
 systemd
Recommends:
 linux-image-generic-hyperv
Description: Hyper-V on Linux meta-package and boot integration
 Pulls in the hypervisor and firmware packages and runs the loader
 registration hook so the system boots into the Microsoft Hypervisor
 instead of (or alongside) the stock Ubuntu kernel.
